    <h1>Buying, Selling, or Transferring Property in the Philippines?</h1>
    <p class="service-lede">Documentation and coordination support for property transfer transactions.</p>

    <p>Property transfer transactions in the Philippines typically involve several government agencies and documentary requirements. FIS may assist with the administrative and documentary side of a property transfer — preparing and coordinating documentation, liaising with the relevant government agencies, and following up on the process — while working alongside licensed legal, tax and other professionals where their involvement is required.</p>

    <div class="service-cta service-cta--top">
      <p class="service-cta__actions">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/contact/?service=property-transfer">Make an Enquiry</a>
      </p>
    </div>

    <h2>How We May Assist</h2>
    <p>Depending on the specific transaction, FIS assistance may include:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Preparing and organising property transfer documentation</li>
      <li>Coordination and follow-up related to BIR transfer processing</li>
      <li>Documentary coordination related to eCAR (Electronic Certificate Authorizing Registration) and ONETT processes, where applicable</li>
      <li>Coordination with the Registry of Deeds on transfer-related documentation</li>
      <li>Coordination of local government transfer-related documentation and requirements</li>
      <li>Assistance procuring title and supporting documents</li>
      <li>Coordination of sale or transfer documentation</li>
      <li>Documentary coordination for donation or transfer processing, where applicable</li>
      <li>Administrative follow-up and tracking of a transaction's documentary status</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="muted">Not every listed item will apply to every transaction. The documentation and agencies involved depend on the specific property, transaction type and circumstances, and are assessed on a case-by-case basis.</p>

    <div class="context-note">
      <p><strong>FIS is not a law firm, tax advisory firm, notary, the Registry of Deeds, the Bureau of Internal Revenue, or any other government agency, and does not provide legal advice or tax opinions.</strong> Where a matter requires legal advice, tax advice, notarisation, estate settlement, title adjudication, litigation, or another service reserved to a licensed professional, FIS may coordinate with, or refer you to, an appropriately qualified professional.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="faq">
      <details>
        <summary>Can FIS complete my property transfer for me?</summary>
        <p>FIS assists with the documentary and administrative side of a property transfer, coordinating with the relevant agencies and, where needed, with licensed professionals. Steps that are reserved to a licensed professional — such as legal advice, tax advice or notarisation — are coordinated with or referred to an appropriately qualified professional.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Does FIS provide legal or tax advice on my property transaction?</summary>
        <p>No. FIS does not provide legal advice or tax opinions. Where legal or tax advice is required, FIS can coordinate with or refer you to a licensed professional.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>What documents will I need?</summary>
        <p>This depends on the specific transaction. Tell us about your situation through the enquiry form, and our team can help identify the documentation and processing requirements that may be relevant to your transaction.</p>
      </details>
    </div>

